I've done a little more digging on this - setting `output.environment.const` to false fixes the const syntax error, but the build is still broken and the export is set to `undefined` for the affected modules. This might be more related to the handling of library exports and the `const` issue is just a side-effect.

I added an example of a [bad build](https://github.com/richinfante/webpack-bug-repro/blob/main/diffs/bad_compile.js) (with the above workaround enabled) and a known [good build](https://github.com/richinfante/webpack-bug-repro/blob/main/diffs/good_compile.js) of the same module into the `diff` folder in the repo - They're minified b/c I pulled them off one of our build servers, but it's the best I have at the moment to easily compare

If I manually modifiy the export lines to remove the `var/const` all together, the module works as expected:
```js
/* harmony default export */ empty_component = (component.exports);
empty_component = __webpack_exports__.default;
```

looks like the unaffected modules all have their exports that look like this (without any `var` / `const`):
```
/******/ 	// startup
/******/ 	// Load entry module and return exports
/******/ 	// This entry module is referenced by other modules so it can't be inlined
/******/ 	var __webpack_exports__ = __webpack_require__(1937);
/******/ 	component_name_here = __webpack_exports__.default;
```
